            <ArticleTitle>Experiences with ioxaglate (Hexabrix) in cardioangiography and peripheral angiography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>673-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 28 cardioangiographies and 24 peripheral angiographies the dimer ioxaglate (Hexabrix) and conventional monomeric contrast media were compared. The general effects of the media on the patients were the same, while the frequencies of pain, sensations of heat and involuntary movements were significantly lower with Hexabrix.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
